      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Analyzing the long-term security for the average citizen, prioritizing domestic industry can indeed ensure a more resilient economy capable of withstanding global market fluctuations and providing stable employment within the country’s borders. This approach also allows more control over national resources and infrastructure. However, free trade supported by deregulation and globalization can lead to accelerated innovation, efficiency, and economic growth. Balancing the two can create a robust economic structure that ensures both national security and global competitiveness. Sticking exclusively to either model risks overlooking the benefits each has to offer, so a blend of both could be the ideal for long-term security, taking advantage of global interconnectivity while fostering internal economic strength.",
